Prepare a bounded, source-versioned evidence slice for diagnoseStructure. Analyze repeated fit problems to identify structural defects. Separate insufficient annotation guidance from real conceptual change, inspect negative examples, and avoid proliferating categories for every rare wording variant. Include direct observations, current authority, contrary evidence, a plausible rival interpretation, and missing decisive fields. Carry forward the actual prior-stage records when provided.
